# OIDC identity provider config for the SPA (Authorization Code + PKCE via
# react-oidc-context / oidc-client-ts). Generic/OIDC-standard — swapping the
# IdP (Authentik locally, Keycloak, etc.) is a config change only.
#
# Authentik's discovery document lives per provider, so the authority must
# include the full provider path (the `<slug>` chosen when creating the
# OAuth2 provider in the Authentik admin UI). Point it at the dev-server
# proxy to keep the whole OIDC dance same-origin (`/application/o` ->
# AUTHENTIK_URL in vite.config.ts, default http://localhost:9000) —
# or at Authentik directly:
#   VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=http://localhost:9000/application/o/fabric-sync/
VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=http://localhost:3000/application/o/fabric-sync/
VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/
VITE_OIDC_POST_LOGOUT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/
VITE_OIDC_SCOPE=openid profile email

# Same-origin API via the dev-server proxy (`/api` -> BACKEND_URL in
# vite.config.ts, default http://localhost:8000). Keeps the frontend and
# backend on one origin so there are no CORS preflights.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
# ...or bypass the proxy and hit the backend directly instead (the backend's
# CORS layer is permissive, so this works too):
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
